{"term":"perk","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9206828de0e619d4f0","definition":"Perquisite.","example":"Free coffee is one of the perks of the job.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":["perkish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3ee983d331bc290edd","definition":"A bonus ability that a player character can acquire; a permanent power-up.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["perkish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:66bf58f9b383096bb7","definition":"To make (coffee) in a percolator or a drip coffeemaker.","example":"I’ll perk some coffee.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal, transitive","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bc6a590b6853cf2adf","definition":"Of coffee: to be produced by heated water seeping (“percolating”) through coffee grounds.","example":"The coffee is perking.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal, intransitive","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:74bc3c00d3c62e779c","definition":"A percolator, particularly of coffee.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:463f13ba313ec6dbe7","definition":"To make trim or smart; to straighten up; to erect; to make a jaunty or saucy display of.","example":"[the squirrel] whisks his brush\nAnd perks his ears, and stamps and scolds aloud","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked","perk one's ears","perk up","perky","unperk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:446035735cea572a45","definition":"To appear from below or behind something, emerge, pop up, poke out.","example":"The heads of plants above the crack’d ground perk:","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked","perk one's ears","perk up","perky","unperk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fd806acec291ee12dc","definition":"To exalt oneself; to bear oneself loftily.","example":"1574, Arthur Golding (translator), Sermons of Master John Calvin, upon the Booke of Job, London: Lucas Harison and George Byshop, Sermon 38, The first upon the tenth Chapter,\nFor whereof commeth thys hypocrisie in the popedome, that men shall preache free will, merits, and satisfactions, and set vp their bristles in suche wise, and beare themselues in hande that they may come perking before God, yea and preace thither lyke shamelesse strumpets.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked","perk one's ears","perk up","perky","unperk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:91b8a6f464f89f4d15","definition":"Smart; trim; spruce; jaunty; vain.","example":"My ragged rontes all shiver and shake,\nAs doen high Towers in an earthquake:\nThey wont in the wind wagge their wrigle tailes,\nPerke as Peacock: but nowe it auales.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked","perk one's ears","perk up","perky","unperk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:829d10f6a4539e083b","definition":"To peer; to look narrowly, sharply, or inquisitively.","example":"He is a tall, thin, bony man, with an interrogative nose, and little restless perking eyes, which appear to have been given him for the sole purpose of peeping into other people’s affairs with.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked","perk one's ears","perk up","perky","unperk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:82ff85a9810bf49e78","definition":"To examine thoroughly.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dialectal","register":"dialectal","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked","perk one's ears","perk up","perky","unperk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b436b383046643d2a8","definition":"To perch.","example":"His seconde hawke wexyd gery\nAnd was with flyenge wery.\nShe had flowyn so oft,\nThat on the rode loft\nShe perkyd her to rest.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked","perk one's ears","perk up","perky","unperk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/pɝk/"},"wordFamily":["perkish","reperk","unperked","perk one's ears","perk up","perky","unperk"]}